Hi.

(I'm an Amiga player with 1 Meg)
Here's another one of my complaints about the nethack game:  Earlier this week
I tried to save a game and it turned out that my floppy disk had a read/write
error.  After about a dozen cancels on an AmigaDos window I got the program to
continue the save but instead of finishing up it stated dungeon collapsed and a
memory request for 1.5 Meg (Which I don't have)  I would prefer to have had  a
message 'save failed try again (y/n)' or something.  This one is the last grieve
and now my mind says that does it, I'll never play again.  After having at least
5 disks crunched to be thrown away I've had it.  This game is really good but
just about every other good effort I have had crashed on me!  Needless to say
this is extremely frustrating.  I've played for two months now and now when the
good games come along I am forced by lousy safety in the program to quit.  Aargh!

Those crunched disks are from this one:  Apparently 1 Meg is not sufficient and
makes the game crash at the end instead of finishing nicely.  So if you die and
press space quickly your disk drive will still be writing when the crash comes
and you lose a disk (and possibly all your bones and scorefiles)  Here is a
programmer's solution for this one:  Instead of quitting immediatley after the 
final press of the space bar have the game wait two seconds.  This is enough for
the drive to finish up so your disks will be saved.  Unforunately I can't 
implement this myself because I can't compile the source.

See you all later, Willem.

Im a King in Moria, Wizard in an LPMud but not a Demigod in NetHack.
